WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
The average person today spends 4 and

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:07.400
1/2 hours a day on their phone and all

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.920
of that screen time adds up to about 70

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.680
days a year simply staring at a phone.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.720
Now, teenagers are spending over 7 hours

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.200
a day interacting with digital media and

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.720
now we're starting to see the

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.920
consequences. The US Surgeon General has

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.880
officially declared loneliness a public

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.400
health epidemic with about half of

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.360
American adults reporting measurable

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.200
loneliness. In fact, researchers say

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.400
that the health impact of chronic

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.760
loneliness is comparable to smoking 15

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.240
cigarettes a day. Now, here's the part

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.320
that really caught my attention. The

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.880
very generation that grew up surrounded

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.880
by [music] smartphones, they're actually

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.040
starting to push back. In one recent

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.800
survey, nearly half of young people said

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.960
they would actually prefer a world

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.360
without the internet altogether. So,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.760
think about that for a second. The

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.400
generation that actually grew up online,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.320
they're starting to want out. So, what

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.680
happens when millions of people start

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.600
craving real human connection again? A

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.800
market opens up. This market could

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.240
actually help the next generation to

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.920
come. If you see it early enough, you

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.960
can build a business around it and

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.360
that's why today I'm breaking down five

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.960
offline side hustle ideas that you can

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.880
start in 2026 that tap directly into

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.120
this shift. Are you guys ready? Let's

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.760
dive in. Small business number one is

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.120
going to be the walking club. Now, this

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.280
is the simplest business on this list

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.920
and you guys might think that this

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.760
sounds insane, but think again because

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.880
there are real people doing this and

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.920
making money. The people walker is a

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.920
success story of an individual who

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.720
started this to help get people out of

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.160
their house and pretty soon it turned

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.800
into a big success. Now, he created

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.720
merch. He hung up funny flyers that were

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.680
eye-catching and relatable and he

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.840
